# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = ["httpx>=0.27,<1", "websockets>=13,<16", "playwright==1.58.0"]
# ///
"""control-cedars: drive a local copy of the CEDARS v2 AWS deployment, plus every check used to verify it.

The stack mirrors infra/cedars-v2. Each piece below stands in for its AWS
counterpart:

  ECS services           backend x2, worker x1, frontend x2, with Fargate CPU and memory limits
  Migrate task           one-off migrate task
  Image build            linux/amd64, as in the deploy runbook
  ALB                    ALB-style nginx: path rules, idle timeout 300, AWSALB stickiness
  Aurora                 Postgres 16.11, schema built by Alembic only
  ElastiCache            Redis 7.0 (OSS stand-in for 7.1)
  S3                     an empty CEDARS_S3_ENDPOINT plus the default credential chain,
                         pointed at a MinIO bucket that is created up front, as Terraform does
  Bedrock                a fake OpenAI-compatible LLM, so runs cost nothing

Every command is non-interactive and prints what it runs (lines starting with "+").
Each one exits 0 on success, 1 when a check fails, and 2 on a usage or precondition error.
Run `control-cedars <command> --help` for examples.
"""

